===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[act#Noun|act]] of [[hide#Verb|hiding]] from [[sight#Noun|sight]], or something that [[cloak#Verb|cloaks]] or hides another [[thing]] from [[view#Noun|view]].
#* {{RQ:John Gay Distress'd Wife|scene=i|page=8|passage=What think you of Flattery, Fondneſs, and Tears? Thoſe are '''Hood-winks''' that Wives have ready upon every Occaſion.}}
#* {{RQ:Blackmore Perlycross|chapter=The Pride of Life|page=417|passage=Here were old buildings, and mazy webs of wandering; soft cliff was handy, dark wood and rushing waters, tangled lanes, fuzzy corners, nooks of overhanging, depths of in-and-out '''hood-winks''' of nature, when she does not wish man to know everything about her.}}
# {{lb|en|Britain|games|obsolete|uncountable}} The [[game#Noun|game]] of [[blind man's buff]].
#: {{synonyms|en|hoodman-blind|q1=obsolete}}
#* {{RQ:Drayton Poly-Olbion|part=2|chapter=The Thirtieth Song|page=164|passage=Whereas the Mountaine Nymphs, and thoſe that doe frequent / The Fountaines, Fields, and Groues, with wondrous meriment, / By Moone-ſhine many a night, doe giue each other chaſe, / At '''''Hood-winke''''', ''Barley-breake'', at ''Tick'', or ''Priſon-baſe'', / With tricks, and antique toyes, that one another mocke, / That skip from Crag to Crag, and leape from Rocke to Rocke.}}

